Guard the <sys/random.h> include the way its call site is already guarded.

librdkafka's src/rdrand.c includes <sys/random.h> under `#ifndef _WIN32` only, while the
getentropy() call the header exists for is guarded by HAVE_GETENTROPY - which configure correctly
leaves undefined on an older glibc. <sys/random.h> arrived in glibc 2.25, so on anything older
configure succeeds and make dies on the include.

This project builds the C bundle against glibc 2.17 so that nothing references a symbol newer than
the 2.19 Kotlin/Native ships (docs/research/research-architecture.md §1.3), which makes this the one
thing standing in the way.

It is a FILE rather than a sed inside the build script on purpose: when librdkafka is bumped, a
patch that no longer applies is a conflict somebody sees, and a sed that no longer matches is a
silent no-op followed by a confusing compile error.

Nothing is reported upstream from this project, so the patch is carried here.

--- a/src/rdrand.c
+++ b/src/rdrand.c
@@ -31,10 +31,12 @@
 #include "rdtime.h"
 #include "rdmurmur2.h"
 #ifndef _WIN32
 /* getentropy() can be present in one of these two */
 #include <unistd.h>
+#if defined(HAVE_GETENTROPY)
 #include <sys/random.h>
+#endif
 #endif
 
 #ifdef HAVE_OSSL_SECURE_RAND_BYTES
 #include <openssl/rand.h>
 #endif
